# ─── Virtualenv ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# This project directory doubles as the Python virtualenv. The venv is large
# (~280 MB) and recreated with `pip install -r requirements.txt`, so it's
# excluded to keep the repo small.
/bin/
/lib/
/lib64/
/include/
pyvenv.cfg

# ─── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ─── Django ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# collectstatic output (regenerated)
/staticfiles/
*.log

# Transient SQLite side-files (the demo db.sqlite3 itself IS committed —
# it carries the demo catalogue, accounts and vault data).
db.sqlite3-journal
db.sqlite3-wal
db.sqlite3-shm

# ─── Regenerated / derivative images ──────────────────────────
# sorl-thumbnail cache (media/cache/) IS committed so shop/magazine product thumbnails
# render on deploy without regeneration. INVARIANT: the committed db's sorl KVStore must
# stay EMPTY (run `manage.py clean_thumbnails` before committing db.sqlite3) — sorl only
# serves a stale pointer when a KVStore row exists; with an empty KVStore it disk-checks
# and reuses the committed cache file (or regenerates a missing one). See DEMO_TO_PRODUCTION.md.
# Wagtail image renditions under media/images/ ARE committed (alongside the DB's
# matching wagtailimages_rendition rows) so the magazine renders on deploy WITHOUT
# regenerating — important on hosts where the media dir isn't writable (e.g.
# PythonAnywhere). Sources live in media/original_images/; product imagery in
# media/images/products/ stays tracked too. Keep files + DB rows in sync: after
# content changes, re-render the pages and recommit media/images/ + db.sqlite3.

